      "textEn": "149\n\nMeaning of the word\n\nNisha-mukheshu—in the evening twilight; khadyota—fireflies; tamasa—because of darkness; bhanthi—shine; na—\nNot; graha—planets; yatha—as; papana—due to sinful deeds; pashanda—atheistic; na—not; hi—certainly;\nIn the twilight of the rainy season, due to darkness, the fireflies were shining, but\nThe stars were not able to spread light, just as in Kali Yuga, due to the predominance of sinful deeds,\natheistic principles cover the true knowledge of the Vedas. Meaning: Srila Prabhupada's commentary is as follows: “In the rainy season, in the evening, on the tops of trees,\nhere and there, many fireflies are seen, and they shine like light, but the stars of the sky—such as the moon and stars—are not visible.\nSimilarly, in Kali Yuga, the predominance of atheistic or evil people\noccurs, but for spiritual upliftment, those who truly follow Vedic principles\nare almost completely disappeared. This Kali Yuga is compared to the rainy season. In this era,\ntrue knowledge is covered by the influence of material civilization's progress. People who create cheap, self-interested, atheistic, and\nso-called religious principles become dominant like demons, while people who firmly follow Vedic\nprinciples or the commands of scriptures are covered by the clouds of this era. People should take advantage of the real planets of the sky—the Sun, Moon, and stars—not the light of the world. In reality, fireflies cannot provide any light in the darkness of night. In which\nEven in the rainy season, sometimes the clouds clear up, and the sun, moon, and stars become visible, in the same way,\nIn this Kali Yuga also, sometimes some benefits are obtained.\nThe Vedic movement of Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu—which is the distribution of the Hare Krishna mantra—is understood in the same way. Those who seriously seek real life\nshould not accept the so-called light of the mindset and atheists\nand take advantage of this movement.\"\n\nHaving heard the sound of the rain, the tortoises jumped up. Those who lie down, the Brahmins are the first to be destroyed. 9. Lexicon"
